Subject: [PATCH] The bank and the docket were two key spaces, and their
 overlap was zero

MEASURED ON THIS BOX 2026-09-24/25, over the live docket and the 111,869-row unrunnable bank.
`judge_coverage` banks every cell whose build failed (88,488 rows) under the judge's own verdict
key and filters the docket by that bank at the one funnel every producer flows through. The
filter matched almost nothing it was built for:

    docket rows keyed differently by the two sides   192,757 of 539,462  (35.7%)
    bank INTERSECT judge_coverage's keys                   0
    bank INTERSECT the judge's own keys               78,771

Both sides import the SAME `cell_id`, which is why this survived review. The judge does not call
it on a docket row: `external_gauntlet.main` folds a non-H1 ROW chart into `params` first and
names the cell from `params` alone, so the chart rides in the identity DIGEST. `_cell_id` passed
the chart beside `params`, where `timeframe_of` reads it FIRST and it shapes only the `@TF`
suffix. Same import, same function, different key space -- sharing the visible half of the name.

Two shapes diverged, in opposite directions, which is why a reader saw a partial overlap:

    chart on the row only      judge GBPAUD@M15.cross_asset_residual.p=6403309d7977b134
                               was   GBPAUD@M15.cross_asset_residual.p=a7abf4646a7e6aca
    chart in params, row H1    judge UK100@M1.exogenous_conditioner.p=4174b6f6734b5405
                               was   UK100.exogenous_conditioner.p=4174b6f6734b5405

So the judge rebuilt tens of thousands of known-unbuildable cells every pass and its pre-warm
failure count never moved (81,588 -> 88,246 -> 109,792 -> 93,320). The same gap silently told
the coverage table that every non-H1 cell the desk had ever judged was still unjudged:
`judged_index` reads the gate ledger, which is in the judge's key space too, which is why
`unjudged_total` reads 450,458 against a 570,592-row docket.

MEASURED AFTER THE FIX, against the same live docket and bank, before any new pass:

    docket rows the bank removes   2,396  ->  81,275   (65,400 of them build_failed)

`frontier_identity.docket_cell` / `docket_cell_id` is now the one row->cell rule, and it lives
beside `cell_id` so a reader cannot import one without meeting the other. H1 ids are byte-
identical to what they have always been -- renaming the H1 canon would orphan every clock.

KNOWN AND MEASURED RESIDUE, named rather than left to be discovered: `lvc_asia_london` is the
one family the judge pins to a chart internally (`_PINNED_TIMEFRAME`), and 721 docket rows carry
it with no params `timeframe`. `frontier_identity` cannot import the sealed judge to read that
pin, so those rows key without the suffix -- which is exactly how `blocked_verdicts` keys them
too, so a build failure still banks and still filters. The miss, if any, is a cell not removed;
never a runnable cell wrongly removed, because the params digest makes a wrong match impossible.

THE TEST RUNS THE JUDGE'S OWN SOURCE. `external_gauntlet.py` is sealed and cannot import a
normaliser, so the rule necessarily exists twice. `test_docket_cell_identity.py` EXTRACTS the
judge's folding lines out of that file and EXECUTES them, then asserts both sides name every row
shape identically. A rule change by one character fails the extraction or the comparison; no
comment can satisfy it (L1.71).

